# Summary
Introduced a TOCTOU race in append_stream_segment: concurrent duplicate segment uploads can cause cleanup to delete shards that another request already committed, resulting in data loss/corruption.
The refactor moves shard file writes outside the PG mutex and delays metadata publication. In append_stream_segment, the code first checks for duplicate segment indexes, writes shard files, then re-checks for duplicates and cleans up on failure. If two concurrent requests append the same segment index, the winner registers shards and records the segment. The loser then hits the duplicate check and calls cleanup_stream_shards_locked, which deletes shards by key via PgStore::delete_shard. Because the shard keys are identical for a given session/segment index, this cleanup removes the already-registered shards and metadata for the winning request, corrupting the stored segment and causing read failures. This race did not exist for same-PG sessions before the commit.

